                <pb facs="0471" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg375"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terres to Mr. Auguste.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31,
                                1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have your favor of March 30. I have
                    carefully noted the statement you have made therein. In reply to your
                    communication I beg to inform you that I have brought this matter to the
                    attention of our minister, who will take such steps as he may deem necessary to
                    prevent our homes being invaded in future.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John B. Terres.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
